    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` with `BUILD SUCCESS` (the acceptance test is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the normalized telephone already belongs to another owner, returning **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the telephone (existing digits-only stripping), it now checks whether that normalized value is already in use via a new `isTelephoneInUse` helper, which compares the normalized form of every existing owner's telephone. On a match it throws `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`DuplicateTelephoneException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` signalling the conflict.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleDuplicateTelephoneException`** (new handler) \u2014 maps the exception to a `409 Conflict` `ProblemDetail` response. This was necessary because the advice's catch-all `Exception` handler would otherwise have turned it into a 500.\n\nThe duplicate check normalizes both sides of the comparison, so numbers that differ only in formatting are treated as the same, matching the \"normalized telephone\" wording of the spec.",
